[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

[b]Troops rise only as high as their teachers.[/b]

You can only upgrade a troop into a unit your party can teach. For each combat skill (One Handed, Two Handed, Polearm, Bow, Crossbow, Throwing, Riding, Athletics), the upgraded troop may not have more skill than the best of the heroes travelling with it: you and your companions. Want veteran archers? Learn the bow, or bring someone who has.

[b]Recruiting is never blocked.[/b] Trained troops from towns, villages or prisoners join at any tier, as in vanilla.

[h1]An example[/h1]
An Imperial Veteran Archer (tier 4) has Bow 100. Your best archer is Cadan with Bow 64, so the upgrade button is disabled and says:
[list]
[*][i]Requires Bow 100 - your best is 64 (Cadan)[/i]
[*][i]or reach clan tier 4[/i]
[/list]
Every short skill gets its own line. The troop keeps its upgrade XP until you can teach it.

[h1]The rules[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Same culture bonus[/b]: for a troop of his own culture a trainer's skill counts as skill x 1.2 + 5 (a Battanian with Bow 180 can train a Fian Champion, Bow 220). Adjustable in MCM.
[*][b]Clan tier unlocks troops up to that tier[/b]: clan tier 2 opens every tier 1 and 2 troop, clan tier 6 opens everything (a toggle, on).
[*][b]Your party[/b]: trainers are the heroes in your party right now, you included. Move a companion out on the party screen and the buttons update at once.
[*][b]Your clan's parties[/b]: their automatic upgrades follow the rule with their own heroes. A blocked target is skipped.
[*][b]AI lords[/b]: vanilla by default (a toggle). Garrisons, militia, villagers, caravans, patrols and bandits: always vanilla.
[/list]

[h1]On screen[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Party screen[/b]: a blocked upgrade button is disabled and [b]orange[/b], with the reasons under vanilla's tooltip. Ctrl / Shift-click and the Upgrade pop-up follow the same rule.
[*][b]Encyclopedia[/b]: the troop tree marks in orange the units your party can't upgrade into yet, with the reasons in their tooltip.
[/list]

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Every rule is a setting in Mod Configuration Menu (optional): each skill, an allowance, clan tier unlocks, whose parties, count the whole clan. Without it the mod runs on the defaults.
[*]Works very nicely with Troop Equipment Upgrade and Culture Equipment Seeder: the gear has to be bought and the skill has to be taught, so better troops are earned. The training check comes first, so you never pay for gear of an upgrade that didn't happen.
[*]Sister mod: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/14526]Item Skill Requirement Expanded[/url] (soft skill requirements on heroes' gear). Together your heroes' skills matter twice.
[*]Only the 8 combat skills count, at the heroes' plain skill. The reason text is English only for now.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859188632]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[/list]
Works with or without War Sails. For Bannerlord v1.4.8. Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
